---
import PortfolioLayout from '../../layouts/PortfolioLayout.astro';
---
<PortfolioLayout view="about" title="About · Ilias Ennajmi" description="Who I am, what I believe about persuasion, and what I am working on now.">
  <div class="gut"><div class="wrap">
    <div class="grid about-top">
      <div class="face">
        <img class="portrait" src="/portfolio/img/face-warm.webp" alt="Engraved portrait of Ilias, smiling" width="705" height="890">
        <img class="stamp face-round" src="/portfolio/img/stamp_round.webp" alt="" loading="lazy">
        <img class="stamp face-post" style="opacity:1" src="/portfolio/img/postage.webp" alt="A Casablanca postage stamp" loading="lazy">
      </div>
      <div class="txt">
        <span class="eyebrow">About · Casablanca</span>
        <h1>Hi, I'm <em>Ilias.</em></h1>
        <p>By day I work in marketing strategy, which mostly means figuring out how to make people want things and then getting out of the way. The whole job rests on a slightly uncomfortable idea: most decisions get made for us well before we think we're making them.</p>
        <p>That idea is also the thing I can't stop writing about. At ennajmi.space I publish essays in two strands. One takes the slow road through psychology and behaviour. The other is the louder half, marketing and strategy, and who profits when people act. Same machine, looked at from both ends.</p>
        <p>This portfolio is the third piece: what that thinking looks like when a brand pays for it.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="sec">
      <div class="sec-head"><span class="label">Experience</span><span class="label">Sample lines · your CV goes here</span></div>
      <div class="rows">
        <div><span class="a">Brand strategy lead</span><span class="b">Company name. What you owned and the one result worth naming.</span><span class="label c">2024 – now</span></div>
        <div><span class="a">Strategy &amp; planning</span><span class="b">Agency name. The accounts you ran and the work you're proud of.</span><span class="label c">2021 – 2024</span></div>
        <div><span class="a">Marketing &amp; content</span><span class="b">Company name. Where you learned what customers actually read.</span><span class="label c">2019 – 2021</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="sec band">
      <div class="sec-head"><span class="label">Four working beliefs</span><span class="label">How I think about it</span></div>
      <ol class="beliefs">
        <li><span class="label"><b>01</b></span><h3>The default is the decision.</h3><p>Most choices get settled by whatever didn't need choosing. Understand the defaults and you understand most of the behaviour.</p></li>
        <li><span class="label"><b>02</b></span><h3>Follow the money, then follow the attention.</h3><p>Every nudge has someone on the other end who benefits. Asking who isn't cynical. It's just reading the incentives.</p></li>
        <li><span class="label"><b>03</b></span><h3>Write to find out, not to look right.</h3><p>I don't write things I've concluded. I write to figure out what I think. If a piece doesn't surprise me halfway through, it isn't finished.</p></li>
        <li><span class="label"><b>04</b></span><h3>Build slowly, on purpose.</h3><p>I would rather publish less and mean it. The same goes for campaigns.</p></li>
      </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="sec">
      <div class="sec-head"><span class="label">Now</span><span class="label">Casablanca → wherever the work is</span></div>
      <div class="grid now">
        <div class="rows list">
          <div><span class="a">Reading</span><span class="b">Seeing Like a State. Scott on how plans flatten what made them work.</span><span class="label c"></span></div>
          <div><span class="a">Writing</span><span class="b">Fewer, longer pieces. Cutting the thin ones rather than adding to them.</span><span class="label c"></span></div>
          <div><span class="a">Working on</span><span class="b">Brand strategy, for a company that should know better.</span><span class="label c"></span></div>
          <div><span class="a">Stuck on</span><span class="b">One Nina Simone record. Pastel Blues, side A, on repeat.</span><span class="label c"></span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="pics">
          <figure class="print loose" style="--r:-5deg"><img class="fr" src="/portfolio/img/frame.webp" alt="" loading="lazy"><img class="ph" src="/portfolio/img/casa.webp" alt="An art deco building in Casablanca" loading="lazy"><img class="pin" src="/portfolio/img/pin.webp" alt=""><figcaption>Home</figcaption></figure>
          <figure class="print loose" style="--r:4deg"><img class="fr" src="/portfolio/img/frame.webp" alt="" loading="lazy"><img class="ph" src="/portfolio/img/tram.webp" alt="A phone held inside a tram at night" loading="lazy"><img class="pin" src="/portfolio/img/pin.webp" alt=""><figcaption>Field research</figcaption></figure>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div></div>
</PortfolioLayout>
